    "note": "Presenting complaint:\nItchy erythematous rash on both forearms for 5 days, also on the neck. Not painful, worse at night. No facial involvement.\n\nTriggers: Recently changed washing powder.\n\nPast medical history: Childhood eczema. Hay fever.\nMedications: Hydrocortisone 1 percent cream twice daily with some benefit. No new medications.\n\nExamination:\nErythematous, slightly raised plaques on both forearms with excoriations. No vesicles, no weeping. Similar lesion on the neck. No burrows seen.\n\nDiagnosis:\nAllergic contact dermatitis secondary to the new washing powder.\n\nPlan:\nStop the washing powder for 2 weeks. Emollients and a stronger topical steroid if not improving."
